      "description": "The reference lists of the papers in `library/`, split into one folio-reference/v1 node per entry with `provenance: extracted`. Each node is `<doc-id>.r<n>.json`, `<n>` being the printed number of a numbered list (so `[12]` in a paper's text is `.r12`) or the position in an author-year one; `derivedFrom` names the section file the entry was read from. GENERATED by scripts/extract-references.ts from the library text, never hand-edited: `check:extracted-references` fails on any difference. The text is PDF extraction, so the raw entry is always kept whole in `note`, and `title`, `author`, `issued`, `DOI` and `URL` are set only where the entry's shape makes them unambiguous; a field the extractor could not read with confidence is absent, not guessed. Listed and exported, with every other `references` directory, by folio-assistant-core's bibliography viewer.",
